A new operator: Boundary Sentinel

This emerged from an obvious weakness in our own method.

Reframing isn’t always useful. Sometimes separating an objective from its implementation destroys the very thing that makes the objective meaningful.

So the new operator checks whether the benefit–vessel reframe is even applicable before treating it as useful.

The current version detects explicit equality in structured inputs. It does not yet understand deeper semantic inseparability.

That’s a small example of the developmental pattern we’re pursuing:

Operator → failure condition → new protective operator → improved composition.

