The workbench’s broader sensitivity run also tested 1,000 simulated changes to our starting weights. The premium hero pack ranked first in 73.9% of those simulations; the Goblin ranked first in 26.1%. Those percentages describe the model’s sensitivity, not the likelihood that customers prefer either advertisement.

The useful discovery is that the decision depends on how we define success.

That’s precisely why the Mirror requires real-world tests.

